      "result": {
        "reply_text": "You can bring a product liability action against a product manufacturer, service provider, or seller for harm caused by a defective product under section 83, and a District Commission can order the return of the price paid along with interest under section 39. You can approach the National Consumer Helpline online at https://consumerhelpline.gov.in/ or call their toll-free numbers 1915 or 1800-11-4000 for guidance and grievance redressal.\n\nKeep your purchase receipt, the broken toaster, and any photographs or screenshots of the defect ready as proof.\n\nFirst, you can lodge a grievance through the National Consumer Helpline. If the issue is not resolved, you can file a complaint before the District Commission where the value of the goods does not exceed rupees fifty lakh.\n\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 83\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 39\nSource: Department of Consumer Affairs - National Consumer Helpline (NCH), H NCH\nSource: Consumer Protection (Jurisdiction of the District Commission, the State Commission and the National Commission) Rules, 2021, rule 3\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
